            "paragraph": "Land-Use Change as a Weak Negative Regulator Land- use change between 2005 and 2020 contributes only - 1.94% to blue water and -4.12% to green water varia- tions. This marginal inhibitory effect is mechanistically linked to ecological restoration efforts (e.g., forest and grassland expansion), which slightly increased actual evapotranspiration (AET) and soil water consumption, thereby acting as a weak negative feedback that par- tially offsets the climate-driven water increase.",
